summary: Package checks under real systemd in a container
description: |
    Run by scripts/systemd-fixture.sh, which starts a rootless Podman
    container with the distribution's systemd as PID 1 and hands it to tmt
    with `provision --how container --container NAME`. Containers share the
    host's kernel and have no CUSE device, so this plan covers packaging,
    the installed production unit and its behaviour without CUSE. It never
    reports guildmaster as operating; /plans/cuse does that in a real guest.
discover:
    how: fmf
    filter: 'tag:container'
provision:
    how: container
execute:
    how: tmt
adjust:
  - when: distro == rocky-10
    because: >
        rpmlint is not in Rocky Linux 10's BaseOS, AppStream or CRB; EPEL 10
        provides it. EPEL is enabled only long enough to install rpmlint and
        is then removed again, so that no test, and in particular no
        installation or upgrade of the package under test, can draw a
        dependency from it.
    prepare+:
      - how: shell
        name: install-rpmlint-from-epel
        script: |
            set -e
            dnf -y install epel-release
            dnf -y install rpmlint
            dnf -y remove epel-release
            ! dnf repolist --enabled | grep -qi epel
